Based on the discussion so far, I will break up my responses into a few

separate posts. Let me second address the wishing section

>  o several possible changes for wishing to include:
>   - what to wish for if you get an early chance
>   - recommending +3 instead of +2 for SOME of the items
>   - NOT recommending gauntlets of dexterity nor of power
>   - should we recommend dip into fountains (or not) to get a wish

[1] What to wish for if you get an early chance

For the early first wish, would it be "good enough" to recommend
 - blessed +X gray dragon scale mail
for those without MR and
 - blessed +X silver dragon scale mail
for wizards and others that already have MR? That combination
satisifies two (MR & armor) or three (MR & reflection & armor) of the
"essentials" currently listed in the wishing section.

After that, should we recommend a good weapon before or after
reflection?

Is there anything else that should be considered "essential" for an
early wish?

[2] recommending +3 instead of +2 for SOME of the items

Based on the discussion so far, there doesn't seem to be a consensus on
+2 or +3. I also checked the wishing spoiler - it says +2 as well. Can
someone make a compelling story to pick one over the other?

[3] NOT recommending gauntlets of dexterity nor of power

I guess I am not sure why this is an unwise wish if you have the wishes
to spare (and have already satisified the "essentials"). From a brief
review of the code, boosting strength and dexterity appear to improve
the effects in attacks (both physical and spell). Are these effects
insignificant?

Please also note that the MAG states in this section
  Having said that, let's focus on the essentials first and then the
nice to have items.
both of these are in the "nice to have" items list (along with a lot of
other items).

The wishing spoiler also puts this into the "high priority" list and
I've already moved it down one level in the MAG.

[4] should we recommend dip into fountains (or not) to get a wish

It appears the consensus is that we should recommend the use of
fountains (after you are buff enough), but I am still not sure we
should be recommending hazardous ways to get wishes in MAG.

The MAG already mentions that a wish from a fountain will occur at
1/150th (or less) for each dip / quaff. I thought someone had done the
math on the chance of getting a wish on average of dipping in the first
20 levels (including with sinks), but can't seem to find it. That would
be a good piece of data. Also, if I read the code properly, you'll on
average get about 15 bad outcomes (nymph, demon, or snakes - ignoring
the preventable bad outcomes) for each wish.

Is it really worth the risk for someone trying to get that first
ascension?

